# Expo / React Native doctrine

This app's screen navigation is built with **React Navigation**
(`@react-navigation/native` + `stack` + `bottom-tabs`) and lives entirely
under `apps/mobile/App.tsx` and `apps/mobile/src/`. Do not introduce a
file-based routing framework or a second navigation library — it does not
apply here and would fight the existing architecture. If you are ever
tempted to create a route-group folder or a dynamic-segment filename to
express navigation structure, stop: that convention belongs to a different
router and has no meaning in this codebase.

- Screens live in `src/screens/*Screen.tsx` (e.g. `LoginScreen.tsx`,
  `SignupScreen.tsx`, `InboxScreen.tsx`, `QRScreen.tsx`,
  `SettingsScreen.tsx`). Navigators (stack/tab configuration) live in
  `src/navigation`. Shared state lives in `src/context`; shared
  clients/helpers (e.g. the Supabase client, Zod schemas) live in `src/lib`.
- Type navigation params explicitly (e.g. a shared `RootStackParamList` /
  `TabParamList` passed to `createNativeStackNavigator<...>` /
  `createBottomTabNavigator<...>`, and typed `useNavigation`/`useRoute`
  hooks) — do not thread untyped `any` navigation props through screens.
- Only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` values may exist client-side. Never embed a Supabase
  `service_role` key, a Stripe `sk_live_` or `whsec_` secret, or a Twilio
  auth token in the app — those belong only in Edge Functions / server-side
  code.
- Store session tokens in `expo-secure-store`, chunking values past 2048
  bytes (SecureStore has a per-item size limit on some platforms). Never use
  `AsyncStorage` for session/auth tokens on native.
- Validate every environment variable and every Edge Function response with
  Zod before trusting its shape (`zod` is already a dependency).
- Row Level Security (RLS) is the real authorization boundary. Client-side
  filtering is a UX nicety, never a security control — assume any client
  query can be replayed with arbitrary parameters.
- Every query must be scoped by `tenant_id` (or the tenant-equivalent key) —
  do not rely on the client to only ask for its own tenant's data.
- Every screen must explicitly handle all four states: loading, empty,
  error, and success. No screen may silently render nothing for a state it
  didn't anticipate.
- Every `FlatList` needs a stable `keyExtractor` (not array index unless the
  list is provably static).
- No placeholder screens and no dead buttons — every interactive element
  must do the thing it claims to do.
- The gate for this app is `tsc --noEmit` plus lint. Both must pass before
  reporting mobile work as done. Never run `eas build` as a check — it is a
  paid cloud build and proves nothing a local typecheck/lint pass doesn't.
